te:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T02:05:12-07:00","id":1248359,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this question has been asked before, but how does the Soul Binding Dread Power work? It notes there is a three dot and a five dot version, but the Dread Power itself ranges from 1-5 dots, so does a Horror need to invest the lion\u2019s share of their Dread Power dots to even gain the base version?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-21T12:49:31-07:00","id":1248486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1248359#post1248359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if this question has been asked before, but how does the Soul Binding Dread Power work? It notes there is a three dot and a five dot version, but the Dread Power itself ranges from 1-5 dots, so does a Horror need to invest the lion\u2019s share of their Dread Power dots to even gain the base version?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it having one to five dots was a typo, since basically all the Mortal Remains DP have the same dot rating logo. Three dots gets you the willing version, five dots gets you the unwilling version. One and two would be useless, and since you don't need to roll for the willing version the 4 dot would also be useless. As we are using Mortal Remains rules, the 3 dot version costs 6EXP and the 5 star would cost 10 EXP for monsters, so a fairly weak monster get it it slapped on top using Advanced Anthema.<br /> <br /> Since it isn't an incredibly overpowered DP, you could decide as a storyteller (or ask your storyteller if you are using it as a Hunter) to give it a discount. You could, for example, just make the theoretical &quot;one dot&quot; version the same as the 5 dot version with a smaller bonus, and still have the automatic success on willing targets. It still won't be particularly practical to weaker creatures (noting willpower spending rules and how many limits the power has), but at least it won't be their only trick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T11:20:02-07:00","id":1251123,"title":"","content":"Does anyone think the Talbot group needs further separation from Yuri's group, as of now they just seem like a more tunnel vision version of them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-03T12:05:05