op=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-22T18:43:50-07:00","id":1262268,"title":"","content":"Long ago, there was a post on onyx path (website) talking about the possibility of hunters being able to recover from slasherdom. Is this still being considered? I for one would enjoy the idea that a teammate can become a slasher with a slim chance for redemption since it adds to the story","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-28T08:16:44-07:00","id":1263195,"title":"","content":"Does anyone on these forums actually play as the hunt club? I just want some pointers for they are played since they are mostly just regular serial killers, not slashers. And I want to know how you take the rulebooks (sub factions) into consideration","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-04T06:30:45-08:00","id":1264595,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m thinking of haveing the alpha kids from Homestuck as hunters but I want to know there stats have any ideas?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 11-04-2018, 09:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T18:38:16-08:00","id":1265183,"title":"","content":"One thing I could not find in Mortal Remains. Does the lucifuge not know the diff between their own demons and the unchained? The book makes it sounds like they think they are one and the same","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T18:51:20-08:00","id":1265185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1265183#post1265183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I could not find in Mortal Remains. Does the lucifuge not know the diff between their own demons and the unchained? The book makes it sounds like they think they are one and the same</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair we don't even know the difference between the demons and the unchained, and we have meta knowledge :V. Their powers work on both, so for all practical hunty purposes they might as well be the same. They have heard about the GM, but demons are the ones who told them that and trusting demons is a rookie mistake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/18090-ruger","name":"Ruger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar18090_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T18:58:42-08:00","id":1265187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1265183#post1265183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I could not find in Mortal Remains. Does the lucifuge not know the diff between their own demons and the unchained? The book makes it sounds like they think they are one and the same</div> </div> </div> </div>You make it sound like there is a difference between the Unchained and the whole host of demons that the Lucifuge deal with, which includes spirits, fairies, Abyssal entities, and more asides.<br /> <br /> The Lucifuge is not merely a kingdom of heirs who rejected their crowns from the Inferno even as their blood flows in their vein, but a hodge-podge of collection of dark lineages where the powersets line-up closely enough to interact with one another and, through them, into the world beyond. They recognize that the Unchained and Institutional Demons (infrastructure and angelic/demonic incursions) are of a different cast than many of the others, but when your purview is a wide net of things called demons, that some seem to embody systems instead of direct vices isn't much distinction.<br /> <br /> That said, from what I remember of Mortal Remains, they <i>do</i> understand that there's a difference, even if it's kind of moot where Castigation is concerned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T19:11:52-08:00","id":1265190,"title":"","content":"So they do understand the difference, but they are still close enough to be considered demons, I think I understand. Would a fractal be welcomed into the lucifuge","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T19:44:47-08:00","id":1265197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1265190#post1265190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So they do understand the difference, but they are still close enough to be considered demons, I think I understand. Would a fractal be welcomed into the lucifuge</div> </div> </div> </div>With a free trip to Milan and a cold kiss from a gun to boot!<br /> <br /> So that actually broaches the weird and contentious part of this conversation-where is the line drawn if the Lucifuge is actually a collection of closely-related-by-theme/iconography subsplats and various lineages, where does Castigation fit into this affair, and what does this mean for the strong core of Hunter-but-Probably-Infernal Demon-ry that is present in, well, both Hunter and Inferno? And, I'll be honest, I don't have an answer for that, directly.<br /> <br /> If I had to take a stab, I would call it a tainting that ties in the relationship between the dark that comes when the switch for slasher is flipped and the relationship ties facilitated by the Primordial Dream covered in a slice of Infernal theming, that certain gifts in the various lines hew dark and close enough that it ties into this collection of sympathies that forms Castigation and therefore allow these powers to bend and direct around to one another, till one bleeds into the other, particularly when guided through the lens of the Lucifuge and L'enfant Diabolique.<br /> <br /> Either way, there seems to be a subset of every single lineage that can bleed into each other that allows them to interact with a variety of entities normally not native to the mortal-human world and the Unchained in an heir-to-power way. This is why one of the big questions for the Lucifuge is just what is Lady Lucifuge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-06T20:00:11-08:00","id":1265198,"title":"","content":"Oh, fair warning-this conversation has been the subject of a couple of <i>heated</i> debates before, so there's odds this also flares up.<br /> <br /> People have some sharp opinions about what the Lucifuge are and ought to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"Arcane