9/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T07:59:35-08:00","id":1473828,"title":"","content":"As a homerule to the Rite of Hecate, would it be fine to allow for it to take blood Sorcery, werewolf rites, and even things like Changeling Oaths (basically anything that's more about manipulating what isn't necessarily innate, in keeping with the Rite being used to take powers that manipulate the otherworldly)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-04T14:48:38-07:00","id":1485799,"title":"","content":"On the &quot;Endowment Creation&quot; chart, there's a two-cross annotation that reads: &quot;If an endowment has an expendable component, such as ammunition, read the number of uses as a cost instead of a refund, and then subtract the -2 refund for being consumable.&quot;<br /> <br /> I do not understand this sentence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 07-04-2022, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-04T17:11:19-07:00","id":1485810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1485799#post1485799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the &quot;Endowment Creation&quot; chart, there's a two-cross annotation that reads: &quot;If an endowment has an expendable component, such as ammunition, read the number of uses as a cost instead of a refund, and then subtract the -2 refund for being consumable.&quot;<br /> <br /> I do not understand this sentence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the preceding one-cross annotation, circumstances that benefit the player should be read as a positive; accordingly, since more uses is better for the character, &quot;cost&quot; should probably be &quot;value&quot; in the terms on the chart, such that a consumable has a net modifier on the value of the Endowment equal to [number of uses - 2], i.e. a one-use consumable subtracts subtracts 1 from the calculation, a three-use consumable adds 1, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-05T09:14:18-07:00","id":1485842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1485810#post1485810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per the preceding one-cross annotation, circumstances that benefit the player should be read as a positive; accordingly, since more uses is better for the character, &quot;cost&quot; should probably be &quot;value&quot; in the terms on the chart, such that a consumable has a net modifier on the value of the Endowment equal to [number of uses - 2], i.e. a one-use consumable subtracts subtracts 1 from the calculation, a three-use consumable adds 1, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha. Thanks. So it should read &quot;read the number of uses as an effect instead of a cost, and then subtract the -2 cost for being consumable.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T18:19:55-07:00","id":1491845,"title":"","content":"Do groups/characters have to buy tactics? I cannot find reference to that, just a list and how to do them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9444-joewolz","name":"joewolz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T19:13:27-07:00","id":1491853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>joewolz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1491845#post1491845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do groups/characters have to buy tactics? I cannot find reference to that, just a list and how to do them</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. There's no cost listed for them in the Experience Costs table on page 74, and Step Six of Character Creation has this to say:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Any hunter can perform any Tactic, provided they\u2019re willing to risk Willpower (p. 135). However, the cells that learn how to play to their strengths will favor certain Tactics above others. </div> </div> </div>If you're part of an organization, pursuing Status can give your cell more favored Tactics that it's more effective at, but the cost of &quot;buying&quot; Tactics is mostly just having the stats to pull them off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T19:40:07-07:00","id":1491858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1491853#post1491853\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nope. There's no cost listed for them in the Experience Costs table on page 74, and Step Six of Character Creation has this to say:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> If you're part of an organization, pursuing Status can give your cell more favored Tactics that it's more effective at, but the cost of &amp;quot;buying&amp;quot; Tactics is mostly just having the stats to pull them off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! I can stare at the pages all day and still miss stuff like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9444-joewolz","name":"joewolz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T12:11:06-08:00","id":1504067,"title":"","content":"Are there any plans for supplements on hunting say...Ghosts, Prometheans, or The Fair Folk, much like the supplements for the 'big 3' in 1E?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T13:33:21-08:00","id":1504069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1504067#post1504067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any plans for supplements on hunting say...Ghosts, Prometheans, or The Fair Folk, much like the supplements for the 'big 3' in 1E?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mortal Remains is that book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T20:43:09-08:00","id":1504100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1504069#post1504069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Mortal Remains is that book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that just the &quot;and everyone else&quot; book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T21:10:06-08:00","id":1504102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1504100#post1504100\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that just the &quot;and everyone else&quot; book?</div> </div> </div> </div>Its chapters are specifically divided based on how hunters typically approach Disquiet-producing created beings, the fae, &quot;ghostwalkers,&quot; mummies of the sort that have tombs and cults, and demons of the sort that truck with the God-Machine. One of Beast's stretch goals added a separate bonus chapter addressing the primary residents of the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> Vampires and witchcraft have a substantial basis from which to address their impact on society and how one does monster-hunting on them in that context, but there's a reason Spirit Slayers split its attention between werewolves and spiritual incursion, and the rest of the monsters that have gamelines about them don't require nearly as much verbiage that wouldn't be repeating generalizable advice from Witch Finders, Spirit Slayers, Night Stalkers, and Slasher.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-28T21:31:32-08:00","id":1504104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1504102#post1504102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its chapters are specifically divided based on how hunters typically approach Disquiet-producing created beings, the fae, &quot;ghostwalkers,&quot; mummies of the sort that have tombs and cults, and demons of the sort that truck with the God-Machine. One of Beast's stretch goals added a separate bonus chapter addressing the primary residents of the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> Vampires and witchcraft have a substantial basis from which to address their impact on society and how one does monster-hunting on them in that context, but there's a reason Spirit Slayers split its attention between werewolves and spiritual incursion, and the rest of the monsters that have gamelines about them don't require nearly as much verbiage that wouldn't be repeating generalizable advice from Witch Finders, Spirit Slayers, Night Stalkers, and Slasher.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Also, I guess with the staggering number of homebrewed compacts and conspiracies dedicated to hunting monsters besides the 'Big three' on this site and a bunch of others, making any more sourcebooks may seem a little redundant...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T17:13:54-07:00","id":1508086,"title":"","content":"Can Hunters have the minor supernatural templates ala. Hurt Locker? Does that answer change with tier? Do Hunters target minor supernatural template characters? What about other minor supernatural templates like those with small amounts of magic or whatever?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T18:07:33-07:00","id":1508093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1508086#post1508086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Hunters have the minor supernatural templates ala. Hurt Locker? Does that answer change with tier? Do Hunters target minor supernatural template characters? What about other minor supernatural templates like those with small amounts of magic or whatever?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Sure, why not. They aren\u2019t too different from Endowments.<br /> 2. There\u2019s no reason to, AFAIK<br /> 3. Depends on the group and the case. Like, the Infected and Psychic Vampires are probably going to get a lot of hostile attention.<br /> 4. Like ghouls and Wolf-Blooded? More likely to be hunted than the Merit-splats, I believe, but this still should vary case-by-case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T18:12:12-07:00","id":1508094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1508086#post1508086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Hunters have the minor supernatural templates ala. Hurt Locker? Does that answer change with tier? Do Hunters target minor supernatural template characters? What about other minor supernatural templates like those with small amounts of magic or whatever?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunters can explicitly have Supernatural Merits the same as any other mortal, and the Lucifuge are specifically highlighted as being no different in this regard in the 2e corebook's Supernatural Merits section. Apart from that, individual microtemplates are going to need individual decisions per table.<br /> <br /> It's likewise going to be down to your group's discretion whether characters with Merit-based templates are deserving of the cell's attention or if they're even on their radar. Characters who are simply Vigilant won't have a mechanical incentive to do more than keep an eye open for characters with supernatural powers if they don't find evidence those characters pose a danger to a human being, but Merciless characters lose Willpower if they don't follow up on the presence or activity of a monster, where &quot;monster&quot; means &quot;unnatural things hunters investigate.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T19:36:01-07:00","id":1508315,"title":"","content":"Can a Safe house be a Van?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-13T20:04:17-07:00","id":1508321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cross-a-way</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1508315#post1508315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Safe house be a Van?</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunter's version of Safe Place is pretty definitely built to be a stronghold; some Features won't make a lot of sense for a mobile Safe Place \u2014 Concealed and Escape Hatch, most notably \u2014 and any such location small enough to be modeled as an object by itself is probably not going to benefit very strongly from Home Security.<br /> <br /> Depending on your table, you might adapt the rule from Promethean (where the characters are assumed to often need to stay mobile and Safe Place is a prerequisite for the Hovel Merit that lets you prevent your Wasteland from spreading) that a mobile Safe Place costs one additional dot that doesn't break the five-dot limit and doesn't provide the benefit of another regular dot (i.e. being mobile caps its other benefits at four dots, tops).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T05:42:41-07:00","id":1508739,"title":"","content":"Am I misreading something in the Endowment creation rules? The example Aegis Talisman build doesn't seem to add up properly with what the table says the costs are dice pool modification. Specifically:<br /> <br /> &quot;If the Endowment modifies a dice pool, the number of dice added or removed is equal to the value -1.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Aegis Talisman adds +3 to contested rolls, for 2 points of value. So shouldn't that be value 4? To get a +3/-3 you need 4-1...?<br /> <br /> Oh wait, maybe I've figured out how I misread it. It's saying the value cost of something is dice pool -1, not that the dice pool is equal to value -1.<br /> <br /> I have a law degree and I don't think I've ever been more confused by anything than this fucking Endowment creation table, I swear to god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 04-18-2023, 08:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T14:11:07-07:00","id":1508777,"title":"","content":"This feels like a stupid question, but is there supposed to be any benefit to buying just an Elixir recipe or Benediction rite instead of getting a new dot in the Endowment? As far as I can tell they both cost three Experiences, so the only reason to buy a recipe/rite is if you have the endowment at five dots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-18T15:17:42-07:00","id":1508785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TwoDSix</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1508777#post1508777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This feels like a stupid question, but is there supposed to be any benefit to buying just an Elixir recipe or Benediction rite instead of getting a new dot in the Endowment? As far as I can tell they both cost three Experiences, so the only reason to buy a recipe/rite is if you have the endowment at five dots.</div> </div> </div> </div>They're the same price, so no, barring some circumstance where a higher rating in the Endowment would be worse or more difficult for you, there is no particular benefit to buying a new rite or recipe without increasing your rating as well if you are able to increase your rating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T01:43:53-07:00","id":1508866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1508785#post1508785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're the same price, so no, barring some circumstance where a higher rating in the Endowment would be worse or more difficult for you, there is no particular benefit to buying a new rite or recipe without increasing your rating as well if you are able to increase your rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought as much, it just seemed weird when I compared them to Requiem's ritual disciplines. I suppose it might mostly be a 'no dingus, you aren't limited to give rites/recipes, just the trait is capoed' kind of idiot proofing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:blue\">Blue is sarcasm.</span><br /> <br /> If I suggestion I make contradicts in-setting metaphysics please ignore me, I probably brought in scientific ideas.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4507-twodsix","name":"TwoDSix","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T18:30:21-07:00","id":1509332,"title":"","content":"I know that according to the fluff, the Lucifuge is descended from Christian demons; would people descended from non-Christian demons (i.e. Jinns, Asuras, Pretas, etc.) be part of the Lucifuge or something else entirely?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-22T18:32:14-07:00","id":1509333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1509332#post1509332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that according to the fluff, the Lucifuge is descended from Christian demons; would people descended from non-Christian demons (i.e. Jinns, Asuras, Pretas, etc.) be part of the Lucifuge or something else entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dark Eras has a Japanese Hunter sect descended from Oni. They interact somewhat with the Lucifuge as cousins - they acknowledge similar origins, but not direct relation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T09:44:22-07:00","id":1509386,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27678\" data-vbnamecard=\"27678\">cybirddude</a> Fourm user lost light has made just that.<br /> <br /> It's a little out dated, but you can still read into it if you want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/866426-strains-of-the-cursed-blood?p=866714#post866714\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/866426-strains-of-the-cursed-blood?p=866714#post866714\"> Strains of the Cursed Blood - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/866426-strains-of-the-cursed-blood?p=866714#post866714\"> https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/866426-strains-of-the-cursed-blood?p=866714#post866714 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> just something that I've thought about while reading Dark Eras. I remember that when Beast's preview was out, I've simply thought about the Otodo as a local version of the Lucifuge- the names may be different, but their powers and nature is the same. However, Fallen Blossom's preview has clearly made it look like it was not the case- or at least, not exactly (I remember Kingsraven interpretation, that the Lucifuge are &amp;quot;royalty&amp;quot; while the Otodo are &amp;quot;commoners&amp;quot;). Things got even more interesting after I finally got Hunter's Dark Eras- The Lucifuge see the Otodo as a some sort of </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-23T12:26:18-07:00","id":1509404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1509332#post1509332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that according to the fluff, the Lucifuge is descended from Christian demons; would people descended from non-Christian demons (i.e. Jinns, Asuras, Pretas, etc.) be part of the Lucifuge or something else entirely?</div> </div> </div> </div>Bit of heavy misundertanding. As of the Player's Guide to the Contagion, the Lucifuge's bloodlines go back to Infernal demons, who may be entities driven to Vice but aren't proofs of Christian theology having any particuar validity, and could just as easily serve as spirits and demons in other religions. Christianity on the whole is no more valid than any other religion when it comes to appreciable interaction with the supernatural. Most instances that would otherwise suggest it are more the result of the supernatural taking advantage of Christianity as a collection of institutions to maneuver within and exploit, again much like any other religion in the world of Chronicles. <br /> <br /> Going back to the demons for a second, older sources make this even blurrier-as of the Hunter Second Edition core book, the only thing that identifies a demon that a Lucifuge has power and authority over are those with the Infernal Dread Power, which could be applied to a variety of things, the Oni of the Otodo are mostly implied to be the same thing as the Lucifuge's demons but manifest just enough deviation in powers to raise a question mark, and First Edition suggested that the Lucifuge's demonic heritage could also have roots in things like spirits, fairies, ghosts, and more such beings.<br /> <br /> Tl;DR, There are no Christian demons, there are demons who will sometimes adopt Christianity as their particular paradigm to haunt and exploit. Those demons could just as easily present themselves as though they were impure spirits under Shinto, rakshasas under Hinduism, tzitzimime under the Aztec belief system, and more, and likely do so as it is convienent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T18:54:49-07:00","id":1509541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1509404#post1509404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bit of heavy misundertanding. As of the Player's Guide to the Contagion, the Lucifuge's bloodlines go back to Infernal demons, who may be entities driven to Vice but aren't proofs of Christian theology having any particuar validity, and could just as easily serve as spirits and demons in other religions. Christianity on the whole is no more valid than any other religion when it comes to appreciable interaction with the supernatural. Most instances that would otherwise suggest it are more the result of the supernatural taking advantage of Christianity as a collection of institutions to maneuver within and exploit, again much like any other religion in the world of Chronicles.<br /> <br /> Going back to the demons for a second, older sources make this even blurrier-as of the Hunter Second Edition core book, the only thing that identifies a demon that a Lucifuge has power and authority over are those with the Infernal Dread Power, which could be applied to a variety of things, the Oni of the Otodo are mostly implied to be the same thing as the Lucifuge's demons but manifest just enough deviation in powers to raise a question mark, and First Edition suggested that the Lucifuge's demonic heritage could also have roots in things like spirits, fairies, ghosts, and more such beings.<br /> <br /> Tl;DR, There are no Christian demons, there are demons who will sometimes adopt Christianity as their particular paradigm to haunt and exploit. Those demons could just as easily present themselves as though they were impure spirits under Shinto, rakshasas under Hinduism, tzitzimime under the Aztec belief system, and more, and likely do so as it is convienent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if demons from non-Christian faiths are real, and the Lucifuge can be descended from said demons, what does the Lucifuge think of hunters who subscribe to religions other than Christianity, like Hinduism, Buddhism, Voodoo, etc and interpret the supernatural through their own religion's lens? Do they believe that these people are fools, or do they accept the idea of other religions having at least some truth?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-24T19:45:14-07:00","id":1509547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1509541#post1509541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even if demons from non-Christian faiths are real, and the Lucifuge can be descended from said demons, what does the Lucifuge think of hunters who subscribe to religions other than Christianity, like Hinduism, Buddhism, Voodoo, etc and interpret the supernatural through their own religion's lens? Do they believe that these people are fools, or do they accept the idea of other religions having at least some truth?</div> </div> </div> </div>2 things are tripping you up.<br /> <br /> 1) There aren't demons from non-Christian faiths, there are just various forms of demon-top down discussion about demons aren't going to be asking questions about Hindu demons or Slavic demons or otherwise understanding them in terms of geographic, national, or religious interests, they're going to go at it from their metaphysical background. The default position of the games is that none of the religions have any more cosmological presence than others-indeed, none of them <i>have</i> any cosmological presence.<br /> <br /> 2) The Lucifuge is not a Christian organization with Christian beliefs. Like, Lady Lucifuge is not a Catholic, Protestant, a Restorationist, or any kind of Christian in particular.<br /> <br /> The Lucifuge are a collection people who have a lineage including demons in the family tree, and the centuries of research into the subject and learning more of the reality of that has become their main dialect. Sure, having emerged from Medieval Italy means that there's an ease with using Christian terminology and conceptions for describing what they interact with, but even at it's earliest incarnation, Lady Lucifuge's influence does a lot to neatly draw the line between the way agents talk about in contrast to their previous religious convictions. Their reality is the demons, not the religions that try (and often fail) to understand them.<br /> <br /> Going with a practical example we can draw from, if/when the Lucifuge were able to connect with the Otodo in Japan, there's not really going to be an organization interest in getting them to identify the Oni instead as devils and the host of the Morningstar-that's not institutionally important to them. The actual point of conflict would be that any demon-blooded individual needs to swear fealty to Lady Lucifuge or otherwise get their brain scrambled, where as the Otodo has reliably operated with having a decentralized system of accountability that assumes more faith in fellow Otodo, even if they aren't part of the conspiracy, than the Lucifuge ever practices.<br /> <br /> So to directly answer the question, institutionally, no, the Lucifuge doesn't give a shit what you name the demons and adjacent angels in particular. How seriously you take any given religion is any given individual's affairs, but the institution's use of Christian language is not a precedent for them having a Christian faith or interest.<br /> <br /> This is neither Scion nor World of Darkness. All the religions are equally empty of substance as far as the supernatural goes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-24-2023, 10:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T06:34:04-07:00","id":1510586,"title":"","content":"Can Slashers, specifically Rippers, have supernatural merits or minor templates (like from Hurt Locker)? I was thinking about having an NPC who has a minor supernatural template who over the course of the chronicle will kind of fall in integrity until possibly becoming a ripper. I know DMs can do anything they want, but I'm curious as to the actual rules. I assume that a scourge can't have any as they are fully supernatural in nature, but if the NPC gets far enough along the road for that to be an issue I can give him dread powers to cover for the merits he's lost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-03T10:04:18-07:00","id":1510615,"title":"","content":"I see no reason why a ripper couldn't take the relevant supernatural merits to have a template. Some of them don't have attached merits because I guess they never decided on one unified mechanism for the lesser templates, but I see no reason why a ripper couldn't be wolf-blooded or a ghoul either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T12:04:47-07:00","id":1514218,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to have a Slasher that only kills people indirectly? Some examples include:<br /> <br /> 1: A femme fatale who seduces and manipulates others into killing for her.<br /> 2: A shaman that commands spirits to kill.<br /> 3: A cult leader that has their followers do the killing for them.<br /> 4: A psychological and emotional sadist that deliberately drives people to suicide.<br /> 5: A crime boss who has goons do the killing for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T14:07:31-07:00","id":1514238,"title":"","content":"Sure. Geniuses/puppetmasters are a good example of this. I will say though, 5 doesn't really sound like a slasher","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-08T14:56:33-07:00","id":1514244,"title":"","content":"Hannibal Lector","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T10:47:24-07:00","id":1514483,"title":"","content":"What Slasher Archetype would be most appropriate for a Slasher who kills purely for fun; that is they see their crimes as a game, and the hunters as players? They don't care if they get caught or not, all they care about is having fun killing people and outwitting their pursuers.<br /> Avengers are out, because they kill for an Ideology.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-10T11:23:09-07:00","id":1514486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1514483#post1514483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What Slasher Archetype would be most appropriate for a Slasher who kills purely for fun; that is they see their crimes as a game, and the hunters as players? They don't care if they get caught or not, all they care about is having fun killing people and outwitting their pursuers.<br /> Avengers are out, because they kill for an Ideology.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quick aside. Any slasher can kill for an ideology. <br /> <br /> I do think you're seeing Slashers as overly specialized in personality. But the easiest archetype would royally be Geniuses","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T09:51:53-07:00","id":1518250,"title":"","content":"I have an idea for a slasher whose gimmick is that they are infected with a fatal, incurable disease and their goal is to take as many people as possible with them before they die. What Undertaking would be most appropriate for this type of slasher?<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T10:07:44-07:00","id":1518253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1518250#post1518250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I have an idea for a slasher whose gimmick is that they are infected with a fatal, incurable disease and their goal is to take as many people as possible with them before they die. What Undertaking would be most appropriate for this type of slasher?<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Possibly as a brute/mask who is silencing the thoughts of his own mortality by killing other people?<br /> <br /> EDIT: could have a cool visual where the longer the slasher lives, the more you see him the more sickly he is, and yet still a killing machine","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T10:22:14-07:00","id":1518254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1518253#post1518253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Possibly as a brute/mask who is silencing the thoughts of his own mortality by killing other people?<br /> <br /> EDIT: could have a cool visual where the longer the slasher lives, the more you see him the more sickly he is, and yet still a killing machine</div> </div> </div> </div>A brute/mask isn't quite what I had in mind; my idea was that the slashers method of killing involved infecting others with their disease in ways such as sneaking their blood into the water supply, rape, donating their infected blood to hospitals (whose scanners wouldn't be able to detect the disease), etc. <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-18T10:38:00-07:00","id":1518258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1518254#post1518254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A brute/mask isn't quite what I had in mind; my idea was that the slashers method of killing involved infecting others with their disease in ways such as sneaking their blood into the water supply, rape, donating their infected blood to hospitals (whose scanners wouldn't be able to detect the disease), etc.<br /> \u200b\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that sounds like a Virtuoso or charmer","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-21T07:50:22-07:00","id":1518427,"title":"","content":"So how would a Brute and Mask Infect people?<br /> <br /> Aggressively Cough on them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-03T17:56:23-07:00","id":1519685,"title":"","content":"Might be a dumb question but would shock collars work on vampires &amp; werewolves? The 2e book lists stun gun/cuffs as an example modded weapon so it seems possible\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","name":"trynmybest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27935_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-06T09:53:53-07:00","id":1519965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trynmybest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1519685#post1519685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might be a dumb question but would shock collars work on vampires &amp; werewolves? The 2e book lists stun gun/cuffs as an example modded weapon so it seems possible\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>You might need to use some high Voltage for the wolves, but IDK about vamps<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T14:52:48-07:00","id":1520237,"title":"","content":"A PC who knew what they were doing they could probably rig up basically a neck-mounted taser. Both vampires and werewolves are tough enough that relying on pain to stop or slow them is a very risky proposition. I think paralyzing them with a big enough shock would still work though.<br /> But you have to subdue them to get the collar on (unless you catch a vampire in the daytime) and then have to hope they can't get the collar off before you can stop them. Valkyrie might have something sturdy enough and sophisticated enough for that but I don't think you could just buy or jury-rig anything reliable enough for long-term use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T19:57:37-07:00","id":1520256,"title":"","content":"I will probably just do it anyway, but can the dread power triggers for tainted places be something a character interacts with in a certain way, such as not knocking on a door before entering causing the trigger to happen, or is it strictly areas within the tainted place have a dread power associated with it, the only trigger being that the character went to that location","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T20:56:06-07:00","id":1520260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1520256#post1520256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I will probably just do it anyway, but can the dread power triggers for tainted places be something a character interacts with in a certain way, such as not knocking on a door before entering causing the trigger to happen, or is it strictly areas within the tainted place have a dread power associated with it, the only trigger being that the character went to that location</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;The trigger for a Dread Power may require a specific interaction with an object, stairwell, hallway, or room; they may also necessitate a character\u2019s specific action. A tainted place triggers Maze whenever someone accidentally trips. A hospital that traps ghosts may force Agonize on a monster who dies inside. A cave may have several, hidden caverns that inflict Blackout on the hunters once they venture further in.\u200b&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-09T21:06:07-07:00","id":1520261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1520260#post1520260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The trigger for a Dread Power may require a specific interaction with an object, stairwell, hallway, or room; they may also necessitate a character\u2019s specific action. A tainted place triggers Maze whenever someone accidentally trips. A hospital that traps ghosts may force Agonize on a monster who dies inside. A cave may have several, hidden caverns that inflict Blackout on the hunters once they venture further in.\u200b&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh dang, can't believe I missed that. What page? And thank you for the answer. I appreciate it<br /> <br /> Edit: nevermind. God, I can't believe I missed that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T15:02:52-07:00","id":1520475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1520237#post1520237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A PC who knew what they were doing they could probably rig up basically a neck-mounted taser. Both vampires and werewolves are tough enough that relying on pain to stop or slow them is a very risky proposition. I think paralyzing them with a big enough shock would still work though.<br /> But you have to subdue them to get the collar on (unless you catch a vampire in the daytime) and then have to hope they can't get the collar off before you can stop them. Valkyrie might have something sturdy enough and sophisticated enough for that but I don't think you could just buy or jury-rig anything reliable enough for long-term use.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was originally just asking in a general sense bc it was some equipment I wanted to give to the third-tier conspiracy in my chronicle.<br /> <br /> The best way I can describe this conspiracy is like if you combined VALKYRIE &amp; VASCU into one organization. But instead of having psychics alongside the human agents they have vampires &amp; werewolves. Who else would know the enemy better? My thinking was that each vamp or werewolf would be outfitted with a shock collar (or some kind of similar device) that\u2019s controlled by their respective human handler. Shock are delivered to alter behavior or punish actions \u2014 just like humans do with dogs. Additional control is exerted over the vamps &amp; wolves via microchips implanted in their brains that are programmed to stimulate certain areas of the brain to trigger specific actions/behaviors \u2014 kinda like ECT.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if it makes sense to do something like this but the idea has been living in my head for a while &amp; I was curious about if it was possible before I invest anymore time into it.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","name":"trynmybest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27935_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-12T22:26:31-07:00","id":1520500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trynmybest</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1520475#post1520475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was originally just asking in a general sense bc it was some equipment I wanted to give to the third-tier conspiracy in my chronicle.<br /> <br /> The best way I can describe this conspiracy is like if you combined VALKYRIE &amp; VASCU into one organization. But instead of having psychics alongside the human agents they have vampires &amp; werewolves. Who else would know the enemy better? My thinking was that each vamp or werewolf would be outfitted with a shock collar (or some kind of similar device) that\u2019s controlled by their respective human handler. Shock are delivered to alter behavior or punish actions \u2014 just like humans do with dogs. Additional control is exerted over the vamps &amp; wolves via microchips implanted in their brains that are programmed to stimulate certain areas of the brain to trigger specific actions/behaviors \u2014 kinda like ECT.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if it makes sense to do something like this but the idea has been living in my head for a while &amp; I was curious about if it was possible before I invest anymore time into it.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>While it lacks the power dynamics you're looking for, I feel like the Cryptocracy from the Contagion Chronicle should be mentioned. As a collection of bureaus interested in fighting social entropy, the Cryptocracy is the faction that is the most interested in maintaining the Masquerade and the general social structures of the world as it is, and has a particular eye for how things look from the human side of things, which can always be argued for weighting towards human leadership. It helps that their Vector, Authority, is one of powersets that works really well without the Contagion needing to be an element of the setting, and in the same vein the Cryptocracy is the sort of group that keeps their united interests more so outside of the same Contagion, so that's a bonus.<br /> <br /> Obviously the biggest issue there is that it kind of sidesteps the entire cruel subjugation enacted by humanity which is kind of the cornerstone of your idea, but I did want to mention it before addressing the original idea.<br /> <br /> So, as for shock collars-uh, not really by going straight at it. While the muscle spasms that's part of the effectiveness are still going to go on with that, vampires aren't going to respond to the pain in the same way and thus be more empowered to tear it off, and while the werewolves have to deal with that pain, they also have a more ready way to accomodate any of the actual damage they'd take when it comes to dealing with it (also nevermind the freedom of shifting allowing for dealing with the problem). It's the sort of thing that's useful as a trap and shock tactic, but not as a long term solution.<br /> <br /> Certain Endowments can be referenced to make it more viable-TFV has an Advanced Armory feature that basically turns the physical forces of the restrained against itself, so adjust that to a collar instead of headcuffs and just make it rapidly retracting, you solve the ease of removal problem-but at that point, you might as well just say you have a Conspiracy that has psi-crowns from Operation Nebula, or build from the Church of the Wolf from Shunned by the Moon, or, hell, just make a them psychics with a weird affinity for the subjugation and control of (certain kinds of) monsters, to a limit. But if you want to try and keep it in the realm of mundane technology, part of the problem that Hunters deal with is that, while a lot of tech can be useful, it's also fallible enough to not be the end all, be all for solutions (nevermind how the monsters can also use it, possibly with more occult adroitness).<br /> <br /> The fact that my initial thought was to instead lean on bomb collars (which is <i>better</i>, but not <i>great</i>) neatly takes all of this into why Hunter tends to lean into overwhelming violence for their ventures, no matter what their end goal is-humans are on the backfoot when it comes to power, and their only real recourse is being willing to jump ahead of the violence curve that everyone else takes their time with because they can afford to. It takes some real strength deal with opposition in ways that mollifies and even subjugates monsters, and that's a strength hunter's pretty much don't have. All they can hope to do, most of the time, is make it clear they've got the shadows at gun point, and otherwise hope they can pull the trigger fast enough if the other side blinks wrong-and that the bullets will even do anything.<br /> <br /> These aren't dogs-and even when they are, they're dogs in the way tigers are kitty cats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T08:05:33-07:00","id":1520525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1520500#post1520500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While it lacks the power dynamics you're looking for, I feel like the Cryptocracy from the Contagion Chronicle should be mentioned. As a collection of bureaus interested in fighting social entropy, the Cryptocracy is the faction that is the most interested in maintaining the Masquerade and the general social structures of the world as it is, and has a particular eye for how things look from the human side of things, which can always be argued for weighting towards human leadership. It helps that their Vector, Authority, is one of powersets that works really well without the Contagion needing to be an element of the setting, and in the same vein the Cryptocracy is the sort of group that keeps their united interests more so outside of the same Contagion, so that's a bonus.<br /> <br /> Obviously the biggest issue there is that it kind of sidesteps the entire cruel subjugation enacted by humanity which is kind of the cornerstone of your idea, but I did want to mention it before addressing the original idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven\u2019t looked into Contagion at all but I have to admit the Cryptocracy, at least from the above blurb, is very interesting. Who knows it could offer some good inspo. Thanks for mentioning it!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Certain Endowments can be referenced to make it more viable-TFV has an Advanced Armory feature that basically turns the physical forces of the restrained against itself, so adjust that to a collar instead of headcuffs and just make it rapidly retracting, you solve the ease of removal problem-but at that point, you might as well just say you have a Conspiracy that has psi-crowns from Operation Nebula, or build from the Church of the Wolf from Shunned by the Moon, or, hell, just make a them psychics with a weird affinity for the subjugation and control of (certain kinds of) monsters, to a limit. But if you want to try and keep it in the realm of mundane technology, part of the problem that Hunters deal with is that, while a lot of tech can be useful, it's also fallible enough to not be the end all, be all for solutions (nevermind how the monsters can also use it, possibly with more occult adroitness). </div> </div> </div>I do want to try to keep it in the realm of a tech based solution because it\u2019s one of the main ideas behind this conspiracy. Without getting into too much detail (we don\u2019t want to be here forever lol) I will say that for the majority of the conspiracy\u2019s history they were developing tech to incapacitate, subdue, and control supernaturals. Honestly the easiest way to describe it is Teslapunk. One of my main inspos for this was the game <i>The Order: 1886</i> actually. But I will look into that Advanced Armory feature as well.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The fact that my initial thought was to instead lean on bomb collars (which is <i>better</i>, but not <i>great</i>) neatly takes all of this into why Hunter tends to lean into overwhelming violence for their ventures, no matter what their end goal is-humans are on the backfoot when it comes to power, and their only real recourse is being willing to jump ahead of the violence curve that everyone else takes their time with because they can afford to. It takes some real strength deal with opposition in ways that mollifies and even subjugates monsters, and that's a strength hunter's pretty much don't have. All they can hope to do, most of the time, is make it clear they've got the shadows at gun point, and otherwise hope they can pull the trigger fast enough if the other side blinks wrong-and that the bullets will even do anything. </div> </div> </div>Yeah to be honest bomb collars was my first thought. But the more I thought about it I couldn\u2019t see it working in the way I want\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27935-trynmybest","name":"trynmybest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27935_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T07:04:11-07:00","id":1523951,"title":"","content":"How much of a Backlash imposing a Condition would be, if Condition is imposed <b>only on failure</b> to use Endowment? I think +1 or +2 to overall Cost penalty is okay, what do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-11T11:58:36-07:00","id":1523956,"title":"","content":"Depends on the Condition. Spooked isn't much of a backlash at all; Madness is a significant backlash.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T16:54:56-08:00","id":1528957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen someone claim that Aegis Kai Doru relics are all Mummy relics because of text they saw in Mortal Remains. Keeping in mind I get the absurdity of part of their claim. Is there any veracity to that claim?</div> </div> </div> </div>IMO it's not that all of their relics are mummy relics, it's that they view mummy relics as relics. They're not going to be like &quot;oh, this relic came from Pangea instead of Irem, it's literal trash.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-19T20:55:14-08:00","id":1528981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was along the lines of my thoughts. Given how long they've existed, I would bet their likely massive collection includes strange and wondrous magical artefacts from across the entire spectrum of the CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Mortal Remains' other chapters use the term to describe supernatural items* relating to Prometheans, changelings, and Sin-Eaters, so it's very definitely a case of &quot;Hunter is a look at the supernatural world from barely more inside than a vanilla mortals game.&quot;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* Including <i>Pandorans</i>, to give an idea of how broad their definition can get.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-22T23:26:31-08:00","id":1529207,"title":"","content":"Does the Code or the Vigil let's Hunter kill Human without suffering a Breaking point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-23T01:35:52-08:00","id":1529213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1529207#post1529207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Code or the Vigil let's Hunter kill Human without suffering a Breaking point?</div> </div> </div> </div>A hunter of a compact or conspiracy can swap out the breaking point for killing a human when encountering such a breaking point in direct pursuit of the Vigil (Page 82), if that's what you're asking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Consumer of lore, myth, history, tales and songs. Pronoun ambiguous. <br /> <i><b><span style=\"color:#9b111e\">This isn't gonna be easy, but the fact that you're even trying says a lot about you. You're braver than you think.</span></b></i> --RWBY V5C5","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25357-lorekeeper","name":"Lorekeeper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25357_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T20:24:35-08:00","id":1529395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1529207#post1529207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Code or the Vigil let's Hunter kill Human without suffering a Breaking point?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on your Code<br /> <br /> Maybe you have a code that says that a monster is anyone that hurts other people, so a mundane serial killer or a cop could work<br /> <br /> Maybe you have a code that says no witness, so you might kill a memeber of network zero<br /> <br /> Maybe your code tells you to kill a monster no matter what, so to kill a mage, you might car bomb a city block<br /> <br /> That being said, while the code will protect you form a breaking point, it can also cause breaking points. |<br /> <br /> Killing someone and then finding out their innocent<br /> A touchstone is a witness<br /> Your carbombing didnt work, and you instead realized you just killed a lot of people<br /> <br /> The Code is a tool for Storytelling a roleplaying, make it your own.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-24T23:42:12-08:00","id":1529405,"title":"","content":"What is the Vigil in Hunter the Vigil? Is it a spiritual thing that can be influence? Or just a mental thing? And does the Code really affect your soul?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-27T21:27:26-08:00","id":1529580,"title":"","content":"It's an Idea, nothing supernatural about it<br /> <br /> It's picking your self up and Connecting with other people, inspiring them to act against the monsters in the shadows as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T16:31:13-08:00","id":1530499,"title":"","content":"What is the benefit of joing a Compact rather than a Conspiracy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-10T17:41:14-08:00","id":1530508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1530499#post1530499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the benefit of joing a Compact rather than a Conspiracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>More freedom and less additional pressure on your Integrity due to institutional mandates and secrecy. With a compact, the most you have to hide from your cellmates in a potential general sense is that there's an organized collection of hunters working together; conspiracies bring the kind of occulted poison-politics to hunter society that lodges bring to werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-11T09:13:59-08:00","id":1530555,"title":"","content":"What Satchel said, plus the question kinda assumes hunters just have knowledge of these compacts and conspiracies when they usually don't even know about them at all","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T16:21:49-08:00","id":1530684,"title":"","content":"Can a Splat use Endowment?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-12T18:58:20-08:00","id":1530696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1530684#post1530684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can a Splat use Endowment?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the Endowment. Relics largely work for anyone who can do the thing that triggers their effects, but unless you're running with a very particular homebrew situation you're probably not going to have even monsters with infernal ancestry engaging in the act of willful rejection that manifests demonic powers as Castigations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-17T14:21:43-07:00","id":1532778,"title":"","content":"Would it be appropriate that a Fetch can become a Hunter? Like full Vigil Code and all? I'm thinking of having that as a twist for a player in my game (of course I'll discuss it with him). I would make it to where, if the character finds out his nature, there would be penalties to tactics and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-19T19:45:57-07:00","id":1532883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1532778#post1532778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would it be appropriate that a Fetch can become a Hunter? Like full Vigil Code and all? I'm thinking of having that as a twist for a player in my game (of course I'll discuss it with him). I would make it to where, if the character finds out his nature, there would be penalties to tactics and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would think so, they have Integrty, Needle and thread be damned.<br /> <br /> Fetches are a lot more human than a changeling. But you might want to make some more Echos for the Fetch to use.<br /> But other than that, and the possibility of becoming one of the created, their really is not much to change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T00:46:39-07:00","id":1534436,"title":"","content":"Does Endowment count as Supernatural Merit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T04:40:25-07:00","id":1534439,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1534436#post1534436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Endowment count as Supernatural Merit?</div> </div> </div> </div>In 2e they aren't priced as Merits nor is &quot;Endowment&quot; listed in the Merits section, so no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T05:57:00-07:00","id":1534440,"title":"","content":"Can other supernatural creature join a conspiracy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-19T14:51:39-07:00","id":1534463,"title":"","content":"The MM was started by a ghoul so I would say yes, they can, to an extent. I certainly wouldn't allow a splat member to get Hunter abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-29T16:36:18-07:00","id":1534922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1534440#post1534440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can other supernatural creature join a conspiracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on the conspiracy, but I would say yes, but it depends<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27385-cross-a-way","name":"Cross-a-way","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27385_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-24T22:54:04-07:00","id":1539187,"title":"","content":"Can you be in multiple Compact and Conspiracy? Whatbabout being in a Compact and a Conspiracy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T05:07:04-07:00","id":1539196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1238405#post1238405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How much does the typical Ashwood Abbey party cost? Not factoring in the bribery to overlook the illegal substances, or the &quot;other entertainment&quot;. When is it being too cheap or excessive, you know?</div> </div> </div> </div>Any ordinary, not-more-than-usually-illegal, party where you're just using Bacchanal (if you've carried that over from 1e) to network is probably Resources 4, or 3 with the Fixer merit, which someone in the cell should really have, so at Resources 5 you can handwave the expense.<br /> <br /> The &quot;special&quot; parties cost whatever they cost in materials, but nothing at all in labor, because you have to do all the setup and cleanup yourself if you don't want to get blackmailed or arrested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T05:30:35-07:00","id":1539198,"title":"","content":"Do hunter get the 8-again roll quality to every single roll?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T06:12:48-07:00","id":1539201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1259318#post1259318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's psychological, and you can always take hostages.<br /> <br /> Further more, creatures such as vampires may have nothing left to continue the requiem. Family is a big touchstone for many vampires</div> </div> </div> </div>One shadow casts another. If a vampire turns Languid from harassment and you <i>don't</i> kill it, it will be back before too long, even more sociopathic. That may not be your problem, but it will be someone's.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T06:37:08-07:00","id":1539202,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cross-a-way</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1532883#post1532883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would think so, they have Integrty, Needle and thread be damned.</div> </div> </div> </div>Every time I read &quot;Vice or equivalent trait&quot; I wonder why there even are different anchors per splat.<br /> <br /> (I also liked Mask and Dirge better as presented in The Danse Macabre for 1e, where they were approximate Professional Training and half-assed Path of Enlightenment.)<br /> <br /> Being a secret monster or living trophy is something that shows up a lot in Hunter, as example preludes or faction secrets. No guidelines about how to <i>do </i>it, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T08:06:11-07:00","id":1539211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1539202#post1539202\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every time I read &quot;Vice or equivalent trait&quot; I wonder why there even are different anchors per splat.<br /> <br /> (I also liked Mask and Dirge better as presented in The Danse Macabre for 1e, where they were approximate Professional Training and half-assed Path of Enlightenment.)<br /> <br /> Being a secret monster or living trophy is something that shows up a lot in Hunter, as example preludes or faction secrets. No guidelines about how to <i>do </i>it, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's partial gameplay so monsters gain Willpower through different methods and thematic to show their inhumanity means they aren't defined by human virtue and vices anymore","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T09:56:44-07:00","id":1539220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1539211#post1539211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's partial gameplay so monsters gain Willpower through different methods and thematic to show their inhumanity means they aren't defined by human virtue and vices anymore</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I don't like it. There's a bit in Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle where it recommends against making characters track more than one Integrity analog? (Not that I know how you would even get into that situation.) I disagree. I think conflicting karma meters is <i>heartbreaking drama</i>, and anchors-per-splat is <i>twee overhead</i>.<br /> <br /> I'm aware that Integrity isn't intended as a &quot;karma meter,&quot; exactly, but I don't like that either. I didn't like it when Call of Cthulhu treated stress disorders and compromised ethics as mechanically the same (it still does) and I don't like it any better in Chronicles of Darkness. It works fine in the special case of Clarity.<br /> <br /> But that's just me.<br /> <br /> While I'm getting things off my chest, it hurts me to <i>say </i>&quot;Sanctity of Merits&quot;. But that's an easy fix - exactly the same mechanically, but called &quot;Hard Knocks,&quot; as in &quot;School of.&quot; &quot;Well, you've burned <i>those </i>bridges - scratch off those Allies and take your Hard Knocks.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T13:06:27-07:00","id":1539238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1508321#post1508321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hunter's version of Safe Place is pretty definitely built to be a stronghold; some Features won't make a lot of sense for a mobile Safe Place \u2014 Concealed and Escape Hatch, most notably \u2014 and any such location small enough to be modeled as an object by itself is probably not going to benefit very strongly from Home Security.<br /> <br /> Depending on your table, you might adapt the rule from Promethean (where the characters are assumed to often need to stay mobile and Safe Place is a prerequisite for the Hovel Merit that lets you prevent your Wasteland from spreading) that a mobile Safe Place costs one additional dot that doesn't break the five-dot limit and doesn't provide the benefit of another regular dot (i.e. being mobile caps its other benefits at four dots, tops).</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think I'd ever noticed that option in Promethean.<br /> <br /> I liked it in 1e Mysterium where you could have all the things that make up your Sanctum in a couple of foot lockers or whatever and there was a system for how long it took you to set it up in a new spot. Could do the same thing with Safe Place and dependent merits. Then, while you couldn't actually use a van as a Safe Place, you could move it in a van.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T18:01:28-07:00","id":1539277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1539220#post1539220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, I don't like it. There's a bit in Player's Guide to the Contagion Chronicle where it recommends against making characters track more than one Integrity analog? (Not that I know how you would even get into that situation.) I disagree. I think conflicting karma meters is <i>heartbreaking drama</i>, and anchors-per-splat is <i>twee overhead</i>.<br /> <br /> I'm aware that Integrity isn't intended as a &quot;karma meter,&quot; exactly, but I don't like that either. I didn't like it when Call of Cthulhu treated stress disorders and compromised ethics as mechanically the same (it still does) and I don't like it any better in Chronicles of Darkness. It works fine in the special case of Clarity.<br /> <br /> But that's just me.<br /> <br /> While I'm getting things off my chest, it hurts me to <i>say </i>&quot;Sanctity of Merits&quot;. But that's an easy fix - exactly the same mechanically, but called &quot;Hard Knocks,&quot; as in &quot;School of.&quot; &quot;Well, you've burned <i>those </i>bridges - scratch off those Allies and take your Hard Knocks.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Integrity deals with &quot;moral&quot; stuff because humans instinctually get conflicted when harming other humans. <br /> <br /> Also I have no idea if that's you being serious or not about sanctity of merits. I only say that because you had a problem with terminology changing in gamelines","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T18:09:46-07:00","id":1539278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1539277#post1539277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well Integrity deals with &quot;moral&quot; stuff because humans instinctually get conflicted when harming other humans.<br /> <br /> Also I have no idea if that's you being serious or not about sanctity of merits. I only say that because you had a problem with terminology changing in gamelines</div> </div> </div> </div>I wish Integrity <i>only</i> dealt with moral stuff. Re-reading, I see that wasn't clear. Take Conditions for horrible stuff <i>happening</i> to you, sure, but shed Integrity only for horrible stuff you <i>do</i>. I love Conditions, they're maybe the best single thing to come out of 2e.<br /> &quot;Sanctity of Merits&quot; does annoy me every single time and I like mine better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-25T20:13:50-07:00","id":1539288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1539278#post1539278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wish Integrity <i>only</i> dealt with moral stuff. Re-reading, I see that wasn't clear. Take Conditions for horrible stuff <i>happening</i> to you, sure, but shed Integrity only for horrible stuff you <i>do</i>. I love Conditions, they're maybe the best single thing to come out of 2e.<br /> &quot;Sanctity of Merits&quot; does annoy me every single time and I like mine better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well that's easy enough to houserule, though chronicles is pretty big on the supernatural being a maddening thing for humans to witness. Integrity in 2nd edition is about state of mind<br /> <br /> Gotcha on Sanctity of merits","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T04:26:55-07:00","id":1539306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1539288#post1539288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well that's easy enough to houserule, though chronicles is pretty big on the supernatural being a maddening thing for humans to witness. Integrity in 2nd edition is about state of mind</div> </div> </div> </div>I've been experimenting with adding a Conviction track to Hunter: the Vigil, working more like in Dark Ages: Inquisitor than in Hunter: the Reckoning. It counts up, starting from 3, whenever you fail a breaking point from something happening to you (external). Conviction can be bought down - &quot;channeled&quot; - for 2 xp per dot. Vigilant and Merciless trigger off its relation to Integrity - Conviction 1/2 Integrity or higher, take Vigilant, Conviction higher than Integrity, take Merciless. When you face an external breaking point, after the breaking point roll, roll Conviction - failure means you take a Condition that non-hunter mortals would take for the same breaking point result, success means that you substitute one of the &quot;mean&quot; conditions from HtV.<br /> <br /> So Conviction is your shield against passivity in the face of horror, but it <i>pushes </i>you. If you're careful about collateral damage and otherwise uphold Integrity, you can carry more Conviction before it consumes you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T04:46:03-07:00","id":1539309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1509547#post1509547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 2 things are tripping you up.<br /> <br /> 1) There aren't demons from non-Christian faiths, there are just various forms of demon-top down discussion about demons aren't going to be asking questions about Hindu demons or Slavic demons or otherwise understanding them in terms of geographic, national, or religious interests, they're going to go at it from their metaphysical background. The default position of the games is that none of the religions have any more cosmological presence than others-indeed, none of them <i>have</i> any cosmological presence.<br /> <br /> 2) The Lucifuge is not a Christian organization with Christian beliefs. Like, Lady Lucifuge is not a Catholic, Protestant, a Restorationist, or any kind of Christian in particular.<br /> <br /> The Lucifuge are a collection people who have a lineage including demons in the family tree, and the centuries of research into the subject and learning more of the reality of that has become their main dialect. Sure, having emerged from Medieval Italy means that there's an ease with using Christian terminology and conceptions for describing what they interact with, but even at it's earliest incarnation, Lady Lucifuge's influence does a lot to neatly draw the line between the way agents talk about in contrast to their previous religious convictions. Their reality is the demons, not the religions that try (and often fail) to understand them.<br /> <br /> Going with a practical example we can draw from, if/when the Lucifuge were able to connect with the Otodo in Japan, there's not really going to be an organization interest in getting them to identify the Oni instead as devils and the host of the Morningstar-that's not institutionally important to them. The actual point of conflict would be that any demon-blooded individual needs to swear fealty to Lady Lucifuge or otherwise get their brain scrambled, where as the Otodo has reliably operated with having a decentralized system of accountability that assumes more faith in fellow Otodo, even if they aren't part of the conspiracy, than the Lucifuge ever practices.<br /> <br /> So to directly answer the question, institutionally, no, the Lucifuge doesn't give a shit what you name the demons and adjacent angels in particular. How seriously you take any given religion is any given individual's affairs, but the institution's use of Christian language is not a precedent for them having a Christian faith or interest.<br /> <br /> This is neither Scion nor World of Darkness. All the religions are equally empty of substance as far as the supernatural goes.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you use the idea from 1e Inferno about Mythologies having an effect on demons, you can make the &quot;closest&quot; demons as embedded in the locally dominant (or previously locally dominant) religion and culture as you like, for the flavor, while still reserving the ability to go strange if you want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T06:32:38-07:00","id":1539310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1539187#post1539187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you be in multiple Compact and Conspiracy? Whatbabout being in a Compact and a Conspiracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm just saying what I like here - use the 1e &quot;Status in your primary hunter organization up to 5, in any others only up to 2.&quot; <i>Also</i> use the 2e &quot;hunter Status crowds out mundane Status.&quot; When one of your mundane Status merits gets crowded out, you can trade the lost dot for Allies or Contact in the same field/organization, representing continuing ties to that field/organization.<br /> <br /> Allow a specific Alternate Identity established for the purpose to raise the cap on one non-primary hunter Status, or one non-hunter Status, on a 1-for-1 basis. For non-hunter Status, this means your Alternate Identity &quot;cleans&quot; your new activities from the perspective of the non-hunter group in which you have Status, and can be done incrementally. For non-primary hunter Status, this probably means you were a mole from the get-go, so really, <i>really </i>don't get caught.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T07:26:55-07:00","id":1539311,"title":"","content":"There's also another way to be a mole - your primary <i>Status</i> is not your primary <i>allegiance</i>. One organization has placed you in another organization, but the first organization keeps you locked at the bottom of its hierarchy and tells you the absolute minimum, so you <i>can't</i> spill much if you're caught by the second.<br /> <br /> Narrative events could also change your primary Status. If you discover the Horror Within or start taking an interest in the terrible beauty of the world and become Enigmatic, well, you might start hanging out with your new friends who <i>understand </i>more than you participate in your previous organization, capping your Status in your old organization while uncapping it in the new, with or without hard feelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T08:08:18-07:00","id":1539314,"title":"","content":"Does Hunter get the 8-again roll quality to everything?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T09:12:12-07:00","id":1539321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1539314#post1539314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does Hunter get the 8-again roll quality to everything?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not unless you're using a definition of &quot;everything&quot; that doesn't actually mean everything. A cell gets 8-Again on the primary actor's roll for its favored Tactics, and things that give 8-Again to specific rolls or types of roll provide those things, but being a hunter alone doesn't give you 8-Again on anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T12:45:05-07:00","id":1539335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1539187#post1539187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can you be in multiple Compact and Conspiracy? Whatbabout being in a Compact and a Conspiracy?</div> </div> </div> </div>2e says one Conspiracy per character, presumably to prevent people from stacking up Endowments. But that's Cheiron Field Research's whole <i>thing</i>, and it must work sometimes, so let's just say it's <i>hard</i>.<br /> <br /> So, on that basis, you're in Survivor's Club and <i>X</i>. What do you win when they find out?<br /> <br /> Task Force: Valkyrie: A ticket to an undisclosed detention facility.<br /> <br /> Cheiron Group: A ticket to an undisclosed detention facility - <i>or</i> a longer leash, an exemption from your quota, and a mini-fridge full of little kits. And you get that blood sample, and the attached after-action form, in, <i>on </i>time, <i>every </i>time. Or else.<br /> <br /> Malleus Malifecarum: An accelerated confession schedule and an admonition about the dangers, to the Order, to yourself, and above all to the youngsters - who are the God-blessed <i>point </i>- of bringing so <i>many </i>bear traps on the Youth Ministry camping trip. Oh, and - needs must when the Devil reigns over this sinful world - if anyone <i>sees</i> the Holy Light of St. Michael shining from that accursed machete, next time it won't be me talking to you, it'll be the Monsignor.<br /> <br /> Maiden's Blood Sisterhood: A shrug and a reminder that good Sisters send in those change-of-address forms promptly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28549,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","user":"Sikander","date":".  Got my Saint wrong 07-26-2024, 04:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28549-sikander","name":"Sikander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-26T21:13:33-07:00","id":1539366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1539309#post1539309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you use the idea from 1e Inferno about Mythologies having an effect on demons, you can make the &quot;closest&quot; demons as embedded in the locally dominant (or previously locally dominant) religion and culture as you like, for the flavor, while still reserving the ability to go strange if you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Buddy, this is a fucking year old.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T01:00:14-07:00","id":1541839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1238403-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-hunter-edition?p=1534439#post1534439\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In 2e they aren't priced as Merits nor is &quot;Endowment&quot; listed in the Merits section, so no.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Endowment should count as Supernatural Merit, at least for the purpose of getting the Supernatural Resistance merit, since it make sense flavor wise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-10T06:26:15-07:00","id":1541856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> 